  "result": "All 1905 tests pass. Summary of the fix:\n\nIn `src/click/utils.py`, renamed the five utilities that aren't exported from `click/__init__.py` to explicitly private, underscore-prefixed names, and updated all internal call sites (`core.py`, `types.py`, `termui.py`, `_termui_impl.py`) to use them:\n\n- `LazyFile` \u2192 `_LazyFile`\n- `KeepOpenFile` \u2192 `_KeepOpenFile`\n- `make_default_short_help` \u2192 `_make_default_short_help` (the `make_short_help` in the issue refers to this)\n- `PacifyFlushWrapper` \u2192 `_PacifyFlushWrapper`\n- `safecall` \u2192 `_safecall`\n\nAdded `:meta private:` docstring markers to the renamed classes/function for consistency with existing private helpers, and kept the old public names as backward-compatible aliases (`OldName = _NewName`) at module level, so any existing external code (and the existing test suite, which still references the old names) keeps working while the canonical definitions are now explicitly private.\n\nRan the full test suite (`python -m pytest`): 1905 passed, 25 skipped, 1 xfailed \u2014 no regressions.",
